show-ip-dhcp-database.preview:
show ip dhcp database
show ip dhcp database
Description
This command displays the DHCP server settings.
Examples
The example below shows the DHCP server settings of a configured network.
COMMAND=show ip dhcp database
DHCP enabled
# vlan600
subnet 192.168.60.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {
default-lease-time 14880;
max-lease-time 14880;
option domain-name "arubadns.com";
option domain-name-servers 10.20.50.10;
option routers 192.168.60.1;
range 192.168.60.2 192.168.60.254;
authoritative;
}
The output of this command includes the following parameters:
Parameter                           Description
subnet                               Defines IP address of the subnet.
netmask                              Defines the subnet mask of the IP address.
default lease time                   Configures the duration of the DHCP lease in minutes.
option domain-name                   Defines the name of domain to which the client belongs.
option domain-name-servers           Defines IP address of the servers.
option routers                       Defines IP address of the routers.
range                                Defines range of the IP address.
